Method: the dispatcher probes `command -v python3`. The restricted PATH below
omits every python3* binary, so that probe fails and the dispatcher takes its
PowerShell fallback branch. A plain `python` IS provided, because the .ps1
twin shells out to canonicalize-sdd-yaml, which needs an interpreter of its own;
without it every case dies on CANONICALIZER_RUNTIME_UNAVAILABLE before argument
binding can be observed at all. Each case is then compared against the Python
master run with the SAME argv: identical exit status and byte-identical
canonical JSON is the proof that the translated PowerShell parameters bound to
the same values.
